Example 13.12: Consider an LTI system with transfer function given by

$$
\forall s \in \{s \mid R e \{s \} > R e \{a \} \}, \quad H (s) = \frac {s}{(s - a) \left(s - a ^ {*}\right)}.
$$

Suppose that $a=c+i\omega_{0}$ . Figure 13.4 shows three pole-zero plots for $\omega_{0}=1$ and three values of c, namely $c=-1$ , $c=-0.5$ , and $c=-0.1$ . The magnitude frequency responses can be calculated and plotted using the following Matlab code:

```c

w = [-10:0.05:10];

a1 = -1.0 + i;

H1 = i*w./((i*w - a1).*(i*w-conj(a1)));

a2 = -0.5 + i;

```
